# Trading Rules & Policies

## Full Filter Pipeline (order matters)

```
Market cap >= $5B (TickerMetaStore)
    → Valid exchange (NYSE/NASDAQ)
    → Price >= $15
    → Volume >= 500K avg daily
    → ConvictionEngine: trend state must be uptrend/pullback
    → Extension <= 3% above 8-EMA
    → Days above both EMAs: 5-10
    → Tradier: live quote + options chain
    → PortfolioAllocator: MILP optimization
```

## Risk Constraints (enforced by allocator + risk engine)

| Constraint | Value | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Max positions | 8 | Simultaneous open positions |
| Max contracts per position | 40 | Per-symbol limit |
| Max concentration | 25% | Single symbol cannot exceed 25% of capital |
| Max account exposure | 70% | Total collateral as % of available capital |
| Max risk per trade | 5% | Individual trade risk cap |
| Max new trades per day | 3 | Prevents overtrading |
| Preview-only mode | ON by default | Must be explicitly disabled for live orders |

## Options Selection Rules

| Parameter | CSP (Puts) | CC (Calls) |
|---|---|---|
| DTE range | 3-14 days | 3-14 days |
| OTM target | 5% below current price | Above current price AND above cost basis |
| Strike selection | Highest strike below OTM target with bid > 0 | Highest bid above cost basis |
| Eligible positions | N/A | Equity with >= 100 shares |

## Day-of-Week Guidance

Backtest data shows Tuesday and Wednesday are the best days for CSP entry. Thursday and Friday entries perform worst. Consider timing entries accordingly.

## Time-of-Day Guidance (Empirically Validated)

Intraday backtest (43,375 simulations across 881 tickers, 90-day window ending March 2026):

- **Optimal entry window:** 9:30 AM - 1:00 PM ET (6:30 AM - 10:00 AM PT)
- **Best single slot:** 10:30 AM ET (7:30 AM PT) — $76.64 avg P&L, 77.4% win rate
- **Avoid after 1:00 PM ET:** Win rate drops to 69-75%, avg P&L turns negative
- **Why:** By 1:00 PM ET, 99.7% of daily volume has traded. Afternoon = thin liquidity, wider spreads, worse fills

The morning window (9:30 AM - 1:00 PM ET) is uniformly strong with minimal variation. No need to time it precisely within this window — flexibility is fine.

## MILP Allocator Risk Weights

The optimizer weights candidates by: `conviction * extension_proximity * liquidity`

- **Conviction weights:** high=1.0, medium=0.7, low=0.3, none=0.1
- **Extension proximity:** 1.0 at 0% extension, 0.7 at max extension (3%)
- **Liquidity:** min(1.0, open_interest / threshold) where threshold=1000 for CSPs, 500 for CCs

## Safety Rules

- All live orders require explicit human approval (preview-only by default)
- LLM recommendations are advisory only — cannot override risk rules
- Kill switch available to halt all trading immediately
- Earnings proximity rule prevents trades near earnings dates
- Assignment exposure rule limits per-ticker assignment risk
